Package: ageless-os-release
Architecture: all
Depends: base-files, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Ageless Linux operating system identity
 Diverts /usr/lib/os-release from base-files and replaces it with the
 Ageless Linux identity (ID=ageless, ID_LIKE=debian). VERSION_CODENAME is
 the Ageless codename; DEBIAN_CODENAME carries the Debian base suite, the
 same convention LMDE uses, so third-party installers can still find their
 Debian repositories.

Package: ageless-compliance
Architecture: all
Depends: ageless-os-release, ${misc:Depends}
Conflicts: ageless-refusal
Provides: ageless-stance
Description: Ageless Linux AB 1043 compliance statement (standard mode)
 Installs /etc/ageless/ab1043-compliance.txt and the deliberately
 nonfunctional age verification API stub.

Package: ageless-refusal
Architecture: all
Depends: ageless-os-release, ${misc:Depends}
Conflicts: ageless-compliance
Provides: ageless-stance
Description: Ageless Linux AB 1043 refusal notice (flagrant mode)
 Installs /etc/ageless/ab1043-compliance.txt in flagrant mode and the
 machine-readable /etc/ageless/REFUSAL. No age verification API of any
 kind is installed.

Package: ageless-agelessd
Architecture: all
Depends: python3, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: ageless-compliance | ageless-refusal
Description: Ageless Linux birthDate neutralization daemon
 A 24-hour systemd timer that keeps systemd userdb birthDate fields
 (systemd PR #40954) neutralized for every human user. It does nothing on
 systems where systemd-userdbd is not installed. Flagrant mode (null
 birthDate) is selected automatically when ageless-refusal is installed.

Package: ageless-standard
Architecture: all
Depends: ageless-os-release, ageless-compliance, ageless-agelessd,
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: Ageless Linux base system (standard mode)
 Metapackage pulling in the Ageless Linux identity, the standard-mode
 compliance statement and agelessd.

Package: ageless-flagrant
Architecture: all
Depends: ageless-os-release, ageless-refusal, ageless-agelessd,
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: Ageless Linux base system (flagrant mode)
 Metapackage pulling in the Ageless Linux identity, the flagrant-mode
 refusal notice and agelessd.

Package: ageless-desktop-mate
Architecture: all
Depends: ageless-standard | ageless-flagrant,
         mate-desktop-environment-core,
         mintmenu,
         mint-themes,
         mint-y-icons,
         ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: mate-desktop-environment, mate-tweak,
            lightdm, slick-greeter, lightdm-settings,
            fonts-noto-core, blueman, network-manager-gnome, system-config-printer,
            synaptic, gdebi, timeshift, firefox-esr
Description: Ageless Linux MATE desktop defaults
 Default wallpaper, theme (Mint-Y-Dark-Sand), panel layout (mintmenu) and
 greeter configuration for the Ageless Linux MATE desktop. Settings are applied as GSettings vendor
 overrides, so users can still change everything.

Package: ageless-maker
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: arduino, avrdude, dfu-util, esptool, python3-serial, picocom,
            minicom, gtkterm, thonny, kicad, freecad, openscad, prusa-slicer,
            inkscape, pulseview, sigrok-cli
Description: Ageless Linux maker toolkit
 Metapackage for electronics, embedded and fabrication work: Arduino and
 microcontroller flashing tools, serial terminals, PCB and CAD design,
 3D printing slicers and logic analysers.
